1. Definitions

  “Software” means the Apiquick source, binaries, docs, and copies.
  “Natural person” means an individual acting in a personal capacity,
  not for an organization.
  “Legal entity” includes companies, sole traders acting in a business
  capacity, public bodies, and anyone using the Software for an
  organization.
  “Permitted purposes” means software testing and software development.

2. Royalty-free license for natural persons

  A natural person is granted a worldwide, non-exclusive,
  non-transferable, revocable, royalty-free right to download, install,
  run, study, and modify the Software for personal Permitted purposes,
  and to make personal backups. Personal use is not use for an
  organization’s commercial benefit or as a paid service to others.

3. Legal entities — permission required

  A legal entity may not copy, install, run, study, modify, distribute,
  or otherwise use the Software unless the Licensor gives prior written
  permission.

4. Restrictions (unless agreed in writing)

  No sublicensing, sale, rental, or offering the Software as a service;
  no removal of copyright/license notices; no claim that the Software
  is approved for use outside Permitted purposes; no use of Licensor
  trademarks without consent.

5. Disclaimer

  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
  THE LICENSOR IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES ARISING FROM USE OR
  INABILITY TO USE THE SOFTWARE.

  THE SOFTWARE IS INTENDED ONLY FOR PERMITTED PURPOSES (software
  testing and software development). IF YOU USE IT FOR ANY OTHER
  PURPOSE, YOU DO SO ENTIRELY AT YOUR OWN RISK. THE LICENSOR ACCEPTS
  NO LIABILITY FOR SUCH USE AND DOES NOT WARRANT FITNESS FOR IT.

6. Termination

  Breach automatically terminates this license. Sections 5 and 7 survive.

7. Other

  If a provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in force.
  If translations conflict, the Russian text controls.
